# Load testing with Stampede

```elixir
Mix.install([
  {:stampede, "~> 1.4"},
  {:kino, "~> 0.14"},
  # Only for the small server below.
  {:bandit, "~> 1.0"}
])
```

## Something to load test

This starts a tiny web server inside the notebook, so there's something to point
the load test at. To test your own app, skip it and put your app's URL in the
load test below.

```elixir
defmodule Hello do
  import Plug.Conn

  def init(opts), do: opts

  def call(conn, _opts) do
    # A little work, like rendering a small page.
    body = for i <- 1..100, into: "", do: "<li>item #{i}</li>"
    send_resp(conn, 200, "<ul>" <> body <> "</ul>")
  end
end

# Only this machine can reach it.
Kino.start_child!({Bandit, plug: Hello, port: 4321, ip: :loopback})
```

## The load test

This is a **Load test** smart cell, from the **+ Smart** menu. It ramps up to 50
users over 10 seconds, holds them for 20, and fails if the page's p95 goes over
100ms. Change the fields and run it again, or turn it into code to write your
own scenario.

If your app runs as a named node, put its name and cookie in the probe fields, and
you'll see its schedulers, memory and processes next to the load.

<!-- livebook:{"attrs":"eyJuYW1lIjoiTG9hZFRlc3QiLCJraW5kIjoiaHR0cCIsInVybCI6Imh0dHA6Ly9sb2NhbGhvc3Q6NDMyMS8iLCJ0b3BpYyI6InJvb206bG9iYnkiLCJldmVudCI6InBpbmciLCJtb2RlbCI6InF3ZW4yLjU6MC41YiIsInZ1cyI6NTAsInJhbXAiOjEwLCJob2xkIjoyMCwicGF1c2UiOjEsInA5NSI6MTAwLCJwcm9iZSI6IiIsImNvb2tpZSI6IiJ9","chunks":null,"kind":"Elixir.Stampede.Kino.SmartCell","livebook_object":"smart_cell"} -->

```elixir
defmodule LoadTest do
  use Stampede.Scenario

  @impl true
  def run(_vu) do
    {:ok, response} = Stampede.HTTP.get("http://localhost:4321/")
    Stampede.check("status is 200", response.status == 200)
    Process.sleep(to_timeout(second: 1))
  end
end

Stampede.Kino.run(LoadTest,
  stages: [{[second: 10], 50}, {[second: 20], 50}],
  thresholds: [{"http.request", p95: 100}, {"iteration.errors", count: 0}]
)
```

## From code

`Stampede.Kino.run/2` takes any scenario, with the same options as
`Stampede.run/2`:

```elixir
defmodule Burst do
  use Stampede.Scenario

  @impl true
  def run(_vu) do
    {:ok, response} = Stampede.HTTP.get("http://localhost:4321/")
    Stampede.check("status is 200", response.status == 200)
  end
end

Stampede.Kino.run(Burst, vus: 20, duration: [second: 10])
```
